      "headword": "אָיַב",
      "ref": "BDB, אָיַב",
      "preview": "אָיַב: verbo ser hostil, tratar como inimigo; Qal, formas flexionadas, usos pessoais, nacionais e teológicos.",
      "html": "<big><big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">אָיַב</span></big></big><sub>283</sub><big><big>]</big></big> <strong>verbo: ser hostil a, tratar como inimigo</strong> (assírio <em>aibu</em>, ver Dl<sup>W</sup>, «inimigo» = <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹיֵב</span>).—<br><strong>Qal.</strong> Perfeito: †<span dir=\"rtl\">וְאָיַבְתִּ֫י</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 23:22\" href=\"/Exodus.23.22\">Ex 23:22</a>; particípio <span dir=\"rtl\">אוֹיֵב (אֹיֵב)</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 15:6\" href=\"/Exodus.15.6\">Ex 15:6</a> + outras ocorrências; com sufixo <span dir=\"rtl\">(אוֹיְבִי) אֹיְבִי</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 22:18\" href=\"/II_Samuel.22.18\">2 S 22:18</a> = <a data-ref=\"Psalms 18:18\" href=\"/Psalms.18.18\">ψ 18:18</a> + outras ocorrências; feminino com sufixo <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹיַבְתִּי</span> <a data-ref=\"Micah 7:8\" href=\"/Micah.7.8\">Mi 7:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Micah 7:10\" href=\"/Micah.7.10\">10</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹיִבְךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 23:4\" href=\"/Exodus.23.4\">Ex 23:4</a> + outras ocorrências etc.; plural <span dir=\"rtl\">אוֹיְבִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 68:24\" href=\"/Psalms.68.24\">ψ 68:24</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 127:5\" href=\"/Psalms.127.5\">127:5</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹיְבִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 139:22\" href=\"/Psalms.139.22\">ψ 139:22</a> etc.;—<em>ser hostil a, tratar como inimigo</em>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 23:22\" href=\"/Exodus.23.22\">Ex 23:22</a> (E, Código da Aliança), <span dir=\"rtl\">וְאָיַבְתִּ֫י אֶת־אֹיְבֶיךָ וְצַרְתִּ֫י אֶת־צֹרְרֶיךָ</span> (sujeito <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>); em outros lugares, o particípio: <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 18:29\" href=\"/I_Samuel.18.29\">1 S 18:29</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיְהִי שָׁאוּל אֹיֵב אֶת־דָּוִד</span>; geralmente como substantivo e, na maioria das vezes, com sufixo: <em>inimigo</em>; de um adversário pessoal, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 23:4\" href=\"/Exodus.23.4\">Ex 23:4</a> (E, ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">שֹׂנֵא</span>; ver <a data-ref=\"Exodus 23:5\" href=\"/Exodus.23.5\">5</a>) <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:23\" href=\"/Numbers.35.23\">Nu 35:23</a> (P) <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 19:17\" href=\"/I_Samuel.19.17\">1 S 19:17</a> (cf. <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 18:29\" href=\"/I_Samuel.18.29\">18:29</a>) <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 24:5\" href=\"/I_Samuel.24.5\">24:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 24:20\" href=\"/I_Samuel.24.20\">20</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 4:8\" href=\"/II_Samuel.4.8\">2 S 4:8</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.20\">1 K 21:20</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 27:7\" href=\"/Job.27.7\">Jb 27:7</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 54:9\" href=\"/Psalms.54.9\">ψ 54:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 55:13\" href=\"/Psalms.55.13\">55:13</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מְשַׂנֵּא</span>; em oposição a <span dir=\"rtl\">אַלּוּף</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מְיֻדָּע</span>; ver <a data-ref=\"Psalms 55:14\" href=\"/Psalms.55.14\">14</a>) <a data-ref=\"Micah 2:8\" href=\"/Micah.2.8\">Mi 2:8</a> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 16:7\" href=\"/Proverbs.16.7\">Pr 16:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 24:17\" href=\"/Proverbs.24.17\">24:17</a> e outras ocorrências; em comparação, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 30:14\" href=\"/Jeremiah.30.14\">Je 30:14</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(מַכַּת אוֹיֵב)</span>; de inimigo público ou nacional, singular <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:23\" href=\"/Judges.16.23\">Ju 16:23</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:24\" href=\"/Judges.16.24\">24</a>; coletivamente, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 15:6\" href=\"/Exodus.15.6\">Ex 15:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 15:9\" href=\"/Exodus.15.9\">9</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33:27\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33.27\">Dt 33:27</a> <a data-ref=\"Nahum 3:11\" href=\"/Nahum.3.11\">Na 3:11</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 6:24\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.6.24\">2 Ch 6:24</a> e outras ocorrências; personificado, <a data-ref=\"Micah 7:8\" href=\"/Micah.7.8\">Mi 7:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Micah 7:10\" href=\"/Micah.7.10\">10</a>; mais frequentemente no plural, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 23:22\" href=\"/Exodus.23.22\">Ex 23:22</a> (E) <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:7\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.7\">Lv 26:7f</a> (H) <a data-ref=\"Numbers 10:9\" href=\"/Numbers.10.9\">Nu 10:9</a> (P) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:42\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.42\">Dt 1:42</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 6:19\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.6.19\">6:19</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 15:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.15.9\">Je 15:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 34:20\" href=\"/Jeremiah.34.20\">34:20</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 34:21\" href=\"/Jeremiah.34.21\">21</a> e outras ocorrências; dos inimigos de Deus, na qualidade de protetor de seu povo, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 10:35\" href=\"/Numbers.10.35\">Nu 10:35</a> (J) <a data-ref=\"Judges 5:31\" href=\"/Judges.5.31\">Ju 5:31</a> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 30:26\" href=\"/I_Samuel.30.26\">1 S 30:26</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 18:19\" href=\"/II_Samuel.18.19\">2 S 18:19</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 66:3\" href=\"/Psalms.66.3\">ψ 66:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 68:1\" href=\"/Psalms.68.1\">68:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 68:22\" href=\"/Psalms.68.22\">22</a> <a data-ref=\"Nahum 1:2\" href=\"/Nahum.1.2\">Na 1:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Nahum 1:8\" href=\"/Nahum.1.8\">8</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 66:6\" href=\"/Isaiah.66.6\">Is 66:6</a> e outras ocorrências; como aquele que possui supremacia moral, <a data-ref=\"Job 13:24\" href=\"/Job.13.24\">Jb 13:24</a>; <a data-ref=\"Job 33:10\" href=\"/Job.33.10\">33:10</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 37:20\" href=\"/Psalms.37.20\">ψ 37:20</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 92:10\" href=\"/Psalms.92.10\">92:10</a><sup>(×2)</sup> e outras ocorrências; de Deus como inimigo do povo rebelde, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 63:10\" href=\"/Isaiah.63.10\">Is 63:10</a>; em comparação, <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 2:4\" href=\"/Lamentations.2.4\">La 2:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 2:5\" href=\"/Lamentations.2.5\">5</a>.",
